# Distance — 2026-11-09
#
# Three distances a reader crosses to reach a thing in Spw, measured in this repo and two mounted consumers:
# reference hops from the canon root, lines back to the nearest anchor, and marks to know before a line reads.
# The owner wondered whether distance into caches or indices could be a design dimension for thresholds of liminality or ephemerality,
# and then about the distance to reach a concept or recognize a pattern through the tree, references and comprehension.
# This entry measures the dimension as it already exists, before anyone designs with it.

#>journal_2026_11_09_distance
#:cache #!observation
#:layer #!pragmatics

^["entry"]{
 date: "2026-11-09"
 kind: #observation
 base: "main@4ec18f3a; the site consumer and a second mounted consumer at their working trees of the same day"
 method: "spw query --selector pathRefs over each repo's .spw, docs, .agents, prompts and lib trees; each ref resolved to a file, a directory to its index.spw; breadth-first hops from .spw/index.spw; last-touched age from git log"
 limits: "a surface with no path ref and no inbound ref is not counted; age is the last commit that touched the file, not when it was written; a second mounted consumer was not measured for reach: its index routes 3 surfaces by path ref, its 313 path refs in 54 files are written from the repository root, and spw query scanned 3 of its 84 surfaces from here"
}

^["thread"]{
 claim: "Distance from the root already sorts surfaces by how settled they are, though nothing declares it. What the root reaches in one or two hops is canon and tooling; the living tree sits a hop nearer than the dated journal; what the root cannot reach is either too new to be indexed or too old to be kept in it."
 two_thresholds: "Beyond the index is two places, not one. In the site consumer the unreached surfaces were last touched 3 days ago at the median: they are arriving. Here they were last touched 77 days ago: they are leaving. Distance alone cannot tell arrival from departure; age or a declared stance has to."
}

^["here"]{
 # 1,276 surfaces; 1,122 reached; the longest path is 12 hops.
 by_hops: .{ zero: 1, one: 39, two: 77, three: 350, four: 343, five: 205, six_or_more: 107, unreached: 154 }
 by_tree: .{
  tooling: "8 surfaces, 1.0 hops"
  harness: "8 surfaces, 1.6 hops"
  biome: "34 surfaces, 2.1 hops"
  caches_tree: "437 surfaces, 3.4 hops, 5 unreached"
  plans: "206 surfaces, 3.4 hops, 63 unreached"
  caches_journal: "218 surfaces, 4.7 hops, none unreached"
  plans_archive: "41 surfaces, 4.5 hops, 24 unreached"
  prompts: "templates, lenses, math, image, domains and sagas sit 7 to 9 hops out"
  never_reached: "agent state dumps (13 of 13), docs waypoints (10 of 10), the v0.2.0-alpha library surfaces counted (9 of 9)"
 }
 age: "surfaces at 3 to 5 hops were last touched 27 days ago at the median; unreached ones 77 days ago; those past 6 hops 110 days ago"
 declared: "3 of 1,276 surfaces declare a #:fixity; here distance is the only signal of how settled a surface is"
}

^["site_consumer"]{
 # 946 surfaces; 877 reached; the longest path is 4 hops.
 by_hops: .{ zero: 1, one: 28, two: 438, three: 295, four: 115, unreached: 69 }
 by_declared_fixity: .{
  stable: "63 surfaces, 1.8 hops, none unreached"
  cold: "6 surfaces, 2.0 hops"
  experimental: "149 surfaces, 2.2 hops, 14 unreached"
  tending: "372 surfaces, 2.5 hops, 34 unreached"
  undeclared: "353 surfaces, 3.0 hops, 20 unreached"
 }
 age: "reached surfaces were last touched about 28 to 34 days ago at the median; the 69 unreached ones 3 days ago"
 reading: "Where fixity is declared it agrees with distance: stable surfaces sit nearest the root and none is orphaned, and every looser stance sits further out. The tree is shallow, so a threshold there is one hop wide."
}

^["inside_a_file"]{
 # From lexed tokens. Depth is how many containers enclose a token; anchor distance is lines back to the nearest #> anchor; marks are operators, particle aims, containers and arrows.
 method: "lex from packages/spw-seed over each tracked .spw file; a line's marks are ranked by how many lines carry them, and a line reads at k when all its marks are among the k commonest"
 here_caches_tree: .{ files: 437, lines: 80033, depth_median: 2, depth_p90: 3, depth_max: 5, anchors: 8141, anchor_lines_median: 6, anchor_lines_p90: 43, marks: 21, marks_for_80: 6, marks_for_95: 9 }
 here_live_plans: .{ files: 229, lines: 25683, depth_median: 1, depth_p90: 2, depth_max: 5, anchors: 521, anchor_lines_median: 54, anchor_lines_p90: 181, marks: 28, marks_for_80: 6, marks_for_95: 12 }
 site_consumer: .{ files: 468, lines: 61553, depth_median: 1, depth_p90: 3, depth_max: 7, anchors: 715, anchor_lines_median: 71, anchor_lines_p90: 274, marks: 27, marks_for_80: 6, marks_for_95: 10 }
 second_consumer: .{ files: 84, lines: 9859, depth_median: 2, depth_p90: 3, depth_max: 4, anchors: 107, anchor_lines_median: 69, anchor_lines_p90: 214, marks: 22, marks_for_80: 6, marks_for_95: 16 }
 first_marks: .{ here: "[ { ^ # ~ #>", site_consumer: "= [ { @ ~ #", second_consumer: "{ [ ^ # . ~" }
 six_marks: "In all four corpora six marks read 80 to 85% of lines, and which six differs by host. The tail is where hosts part: 9 marks reach 95% in the caches tree and 16 in the second consumer."
 address: "The caches tree puts an anchor within 6 lines of the median line, so a citation lands on the claim. Everywhere else the nearest anchor is 54 to 71 lines back, so a citation lands on a file."
 shallow: "Nothing is deep. Nine tokens in ten sit within three containers in every corpus; distance in Spw is mostly sideways, through references, and not downward."
 unread_as_plans: "24% of lines in live plans sit above any anchor, in the card and its frames, which are addressed by frame name and not by #>"
}

^["from_a_centre"]{
 # Reach measured from any surface a reader holds, and the cycles the references make. Same refs, a different origin.
 method: "the same resolved refs, walked breadth-first from a chosen surface, outward by what it cites and inward by what cites it; cycles as strongly connected groups of surfaces"
 walk_cost: "0.1 to 3.2 ms per centre over 5,176 edges here and 5,785 in the site consumer"
 rings_here: .{ canon_root: "out 39, 77, 350, 343; in 8, 20, 29, 48", a_live_plan: "out 7, 29, 57, 81; in 6, 16, 34, 54", a_theory_surface: "out 10, 35, 82, 131; in 1, 6, 20, 31", a_journal_entry: "out none; in 2, 4, 17, 31", an_archived_plan: "out 4, 8, 23, 47; in 1, 1, none" }
 eddies_here: "13 groups in which every surface reaches every other, holding 652 of 1,222 surfaces; the largest holds 363, of which 361 are the living caches tree; the next holds 250; 494 pairs of surfaces cite each other"
 eddies_site: "one group holds 769 of 939 surfaces; 745 pairs cite each other"
 reading: "A journal entry is cited and cites nothing that returns, so it sits outside every cycle: a record. The living tree is one eddy: every surface in it can be reached from every other, which is what staying true together looks like in a graph. An archived plan still points outward and is almost never pointed at: it is leaving."
 two_origins: "Hops from the root say how settled a thing is. Hops from the held surface say what is near the reader now. They are different distances with the same unit."
}

^["readings"]{
 reach: "hops from the root: how many doors a reader opens before a surface, and so how much context they carry in"
 two_edges: "the index has an inner edge a surface crosses when it is first routed, and an outer edge it crosses when its route is dropped; both leave it unreached"
 layers_by_clock: "the retention planes in docs/theory/spw/cache-field.spw are distances in time (8, 64 and 256 beats); hops are the same idea in space"
 not_a_law: "a deep surface is not a doubtful one: prompts sit 7 to 9 hops out because they chain, and are old and stable"
 three_kinds: "hops are crossed by following, anchor lines by scrolling, marks by learning; a tool can shorten the first two, and only practice shortens the third"
}

^["follows"]{
 theory: ~"../../../docs/theory/spw/threshold-distance.spw"
 trials: ~"../../../.agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw"
 held: "Nothing was changed by this measure. The scripts were scratch; a reach column in spw census or spw graph would make it repeatable."
}
